<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakhstan oil production falls in October.</title>
<headline>Kazakhstan oil production falls in October.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakhstan's production of crude oil and gas condensate fell in October to 1.88 million tonnes from almost 2.00 million in September, the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The committee released the following figures for energy output in its latest monthly statistical review:</p>
<p> KAZAKH ENERGY OUTPUT	    Oct	 Sept	 Jan-Oct 96</p>
<p> Crude oil (million tonnes)    1.880     1.996	   18.562</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	    -5.8	 +/0		n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	    +2.0     +17.0	    +10.9</p>
<p>Natural gas</p>
<p>  (billion cubic metres)	 0.52	0.53	     5.1</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	    -2.8	+1.6		n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	    -5.4     +18.5	     +6.9</p>
<p> Gasoline (tonnes)	     112,800   233,200	1,963,300</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct changed	  -51.6	+3.0		n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	   -36.6     +12.9	    +13.0</p>
<p> Diesel (tonnes)		 239,000   368,000	2,860,200</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	   -35.1     +14.7		n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr change		   -14.7	+9.8	     +4.0</p>
<p>  Fuel oil (mazut) (tonnes)  336,000   373,600	3,108,700</p>
<p>   mth/mth pct change	  -10.1     +29.9		n/a</p>
<p>   yr/yr pct change	     +0.2	+3.1	     +3.8</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom +7 327 509410</p>
</text>
